From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Exit when a stream is stopped before portal setup completes

SIGTERM may arrive before the portal callback has installed a sink state
handler. Stopping the sink alone then leaves the process alive indefinitely.
Cancel pending setup, stop the sink when present, and always quit the
application.

--- a/src/stream/nd-stream.c
+++ b/src/stream/nd-stream.c
@@ -553,7 +553,16 @@
 {
   g_debug ("NdStream: Received %s signal. Exiting...", signal_name);
 
-  nd_sink_stop_stream (self->sink);
+  if (self->cancellable)
+    g_cancellable_cancel (self->cancellable);
+
+  if (self->sink)
+    nd_sink_stop_stream (self->sink);
+
+  /* A signal can arrive before the portal session has completed. In that
+   * case no sink state handler is connected yet, so stopping the sink alone
+   * does not cause the application to exit. */
+  g_application_quit (G_APPLICATION (self));
 
   return G_SOURCE_REMOVE;
 }
